# Core factors in the binary distance-eight branch

The built partial argument places H inside the core's fixed factor, places
U join H in the core center, and proves U and H disjoint, using the explicit
centrality conclusion of (4.4). The source's three nested orbit layers and
its precise preceding inputs are exported for the remaining local and
quotient arguments.

The order-four result, fixed-factor equality and reverse center inclusion
remain unfinished. This module does not assert (4.5)(iii--iv).

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.895--900.
-/
